# Freeze in Place on an already tapped creature (the ruling, CR 701.26a, 122.1d): Bot2's Ornithopter attacks on turn 4 and is still tapped on turn 5, when
# Bot1 casts Freeze in Place on it: it stays tapped and still gets three stun counters, and the scry still happens (the Library's top card goes to the bottom).

[Bot1 Deck]
Freeze in Place
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Freeze in Place.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange( | Lightning Bolt; Counterspell)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Freeze in Place
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = 3
Bot1.Library.Top = Island
Stack.Count = 0
